<title>GERMANY: SGL Carbon sees oper profit over 300 mln DM.</title>
<headline>SGL Carbon sees oper profit over 300 mln DM.</headline>
<dateline>WILDBAD KREUTH, Germany 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>German graphite producer SGL Carbon said on Wednesday it expected 1996 operating profit to exceed 300 million marks ($190.3 million), surpassing the previous year's 260 million marks.</p>
<p>The gain would mark a turnaround in results for the company, chief executive Robert Koehler said on Thursday at a meeting of Germany's Christian Social Union political party.</p>
<p>SGL Carbon in November reported a 24 percent hike in nine-month operating profits to 231 million marks.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, (49-228) 260 97 150 ($ = 1.576 German Marks)</p>
</text>
